# Recruiter Threads

One section per active or recent recruiter conversation. The heading is the recruiter's name and firm; the body captures whatever's worth remembering about the thread. There's no enforced schema, but consistent fields help the skill surface useful excerpts.

Mark a thread "closed" or "lapsed" rather than deleting it — context survives the next time the recruiter or one of their clients resurfaces.

## Jane Recruiter — ExampleFirm Search Partners

- **Title:** Sr. Executive Recruiter, ExampleFirm (she/her)
- **LinkedIn:** linkedin.com/in/janerecruiter/
- **First contact:** Cold DM 2026-04-12
- **Role pitched:** {Target Company} — Director of Engineering, Platform (Hybrid NYC, reports to VP Eng)
- **First call:** 2026-04-17 11:00–11:30 AM ET
- **Strongest signals:** Stack matches resume; team-size scope matches recent role.
- **Comp anchor:** Base $X–$Y, bonus Z%, plus equity. Total target $T.
- **Status:** Active — paper-screen submitted 2026-04-19, awaiting feedback.
- **Notes:** Prefers candidates who can be hands-on through the first 90 days; wants to see a "before/after" architecture artifact.

